Subject: [PATCH] navsim_v1: keep each camera's image path, as navsim v2 does

Paddock's NAVSIM proxy agent ships image *paths* to the model node rather than
pixels: the scorer and the node share a filesystem, and re-sending one
1920x1080 history frame per camera over a socket would move ~8 GB across 242
scenarios. Upstream navsim v2 added `Camera.camera_path` for exactly this, and
the proxy reads it. navsim v1.1 opens the JPEG inside `Cameras.from_camera_dict`
and discards the path, and `AgentInput` offers no other route to it, so it
cannot be recovered outside the devkit.

Additive: an Optional field defaulting to None, populated where the image is
loaded. Nothing in the v1 devkit reads it. Same field name as v2's so one proxy
serves both devkits. Not upstreamable in practice: navsim v1 is unmaintained
and v2 already has it.

---
diff --git a/navsim_v1/navsim/common/dataclasses.py b/navsim_v1/navsim/common/dataclasses.py
index 0f4671c..8484244 100755
--- a/navsim_v1/navsim/common/dataclasses.py
+++ b/navsim_v1/navsim/common/dataclasses.py
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@ class Camera:
     sensor2lidar_translation: Optional[npt.NDArray[np.float32]] = None
     intrinsics: Optional[npt.NDArray[np.float32]] = None
     distortion: Optional[npt.NDArray[np.float32]] = None
+    camera_path: Optional[Path] = None
 
 
 @dataclass
@@ -79,6 +80,7 @@ class Cameras:
                     sensor2lidar_translation=camera_dict[camera_name]["sensor2lidar_translation"],
                     intrinsics=camera_dict[camera_name]["cam_intrinsic"],
                     distortion=camera_dict[camera_name]["distortion"],
+                    camera_path=camera_dict[camera_name]["data_path"],
                 )
             else:
                 data_dict[camera_identifier] = Camera()  # empty camera
